0016>. Let <MATH_0017>\nbe the submodule of trivial relations, i.e., the submodule of <MATH_0018>\ngenerated by the elements <MATH_0019>.\nConsider the complex of <MATH_0020>-modules\n<MATH_0021>\nwhere the last term is placed in degree <MATH_0022>. The first map is the obvious\none and the second map sends the basis element corresponding to <MATH_0023>\nto <MATH_0024>.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:8cdc9babc32d7d512932ed555edcf9aeac5783290d15c3e4238c2a6a0f587fdb", "unit_id": "tag:09AM:prose-0001"}
